{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Mixpanel project through its track API."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-to-Mixpanel","title":"Sending to Mixpanel","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/mixpanel","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError"]},{"anchor":"Encoding-batches","title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder"]},{"anchor":"Records-left-out","title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"text":" makes an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"text":") for your Mixpanel project in one call. It checks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the project token, posts to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/track","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" endpoint of the project’s data residency","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion"},{"text":"), with ","type":"text"},{"code":"verbose=1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", through a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder"},{"text":", and splits each batch to Mixpanel’s limits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"text":"): 2,000 events and 2 MB a request. A batch with no record the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It retries no response, a 5xx, 408","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and 429, waiting ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/mixpanel"},{"text":": Mixpanel’s recommended","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule, 2 s doubling to 60 s. The full jitter on top is Traffluent’s own choice. It drops and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reports any other status. The token goes in each event, so no header field is needed, and no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leaves this module out; import it on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The project token is public: Mixpanel’s own apps and web pages ship it. The destination takes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nothing else. Never put the project’s secret or a service account’s credentials in an app; they","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"belong to Mixpanel’s import API, for servers. The factory throws ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"empty token, and for one with a character other than a letter or digit, which no project token","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The region has no default. A project’s data resides in the US, the EU or India, and Mixpanel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ingests nothing for it from another residency’s endpoint, so you pick the region on purpose."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record becomes an event of an anonymous user. Its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"text":" is the record’s session,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the sessions enricher, also sent as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_id"},{"text":"; a record with no session is sent under its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own record identifier, with no ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device_id"},{"text":". Under Simplified ID Merge, Mixpanel shows a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"session’s events under ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$device:<session>"},{"text":", and a sessionless record’s under its bare record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier. No ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$user_id"},{"text":" is sent. Its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$insert_id"},{"text":" is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps, and its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"text":" the record’s timestamp in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"epoch milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent. Each event’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"text":", as is the endpoint’s, so Mixpanel adds no location from the request’s address. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"standard context is sent as Mixpanel’s default properties (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_version_string"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$app_build_number"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$model"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$wifi"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$os_version"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Mixpanel counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"text":", so each session is one user in its reports, and so is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each record sent without a session. On a Mixpanel plan billed by monthly tracked users, each counts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as one.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TrackingPlan"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the encoder can’t write is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"starts with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":", as Mixpanel’s own events’ names do, one with a property Mixpanel reads for itself"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":"-prefixed one, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"time"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ip"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bucket"},{"type":"text","text":"), one of 255 properties or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"more counting the encoder’s own, one holding an array of 255 elements or more, one whose property"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nests objects more than 3 deep, one whose event isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp is before 1971 or has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"epoch-milliseconds form, and one too large for Mixpanel. The destination reports each as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel answers 200 even when it finds no valid event in a request. The endpoint asks for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verbose=1"},{"type":"text","text":", so the answer’s body says so, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{\"status\": 0, \"error\": ...}"},{"type":"text","text":", and the destination"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"drops the request and reports it as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDropReport.rejectedInBody(status:reason:recordIDs:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with Mixpanel’s error as the reason. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"status"},{"type":"text","text":" of 1 means only that one event or more was well"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"formed: it doesn’t confirm that the token names a project, so a wrong region, or a token of no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"project, may be answered 200 with nothing stored. Check the project’s Live View after setting the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination up. Its track API ingests only events from the last 5 days, so a record older than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that when it is sent isn’t stored, and is reported only when no event of its request was valid."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to PostHog or Amplitude, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"AmplitudeEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import MixpanelEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let mixpanel = try HTTPDestination.mixpanel(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu or .india, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: mixpanel)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers what Mixpanel receives, and why, in more detail.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"externalID":"MixpanelEncoding","modules":[{"name":"MixpanelEncoding"}],"symbolKind":"module","role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework","title":"MixpanelEncoding"},"references":{"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelBatchEncoder":{"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" of Mixpanel’s track API, so an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can send","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events to a Mixpanel project’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/track","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MixpanelBatchEncoder","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelbatchencoder"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Mixpanel project through its track API."}],"title":"MixpanelEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelEncodingError":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MixpanelEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelencodingerror","title":"MixpanelEncodingError","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requests as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for the batch."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MixpanelEncodingError","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/HTTPDestinations/ExponentialBackoff/mixpanel":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel’s recommended schedule, 2 s doubling to 60 s, with full jitter: a nominal wait of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"2 seconds before the first retry, doubling up to 60 seconds. Mixpanel recommends the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schedule; the full jitter is Traffluent’s, as for every destination."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/mixpanel","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mixpanel"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations18ExponentialBackoffV","text":"ExponentialBackoff"}],"title":"mixpanel","role":"symbol","url":"\/do